---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="A task takes several steps, each of which can fail. Choose the steps, the reliability of each step and whether each result is checked and retried once, and see the chance that the whole task succeeds and how many tokens are read when the whole history is re-read at every step. The reliability is a rate you set, and steps are treated as independent. A retry assumes a check that catches every failed step and a second try that fails independently; the cost of the check itself is not counted.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with the defaults: <b>Steps in the task</b> <b>8</b>, <b>Success of each step</b> <b>95</b>, <b>Check and retry each step</b> <b>No</b> and <b>Tokens added per step</b> <b>500</b>. The whole task succeeds <b>66.3</b> percent of the time, <b>18000</b> tokens are read in total, and the model is called <b>8</b> times.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Check and retry each step</b> to <b>Yes, one retry</b>: the task now succeeds <b>98.0</b> percent of the time, and the model is called <b>8.4</b> times on average. A little extra work buys a lot of reliability.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Check and retry each step</b> back to <b>No</b> and <b>Steps in the task</b> to <b>20</b>: success falls to <b>35.8</b> percent, and the tokens read rise to <b>105000</b>, more than five times those of 8 steps, since the history is re-read each time.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Success of each step</b> to <b>99</b>: success rises to <b>81.8</b> percent. Small gains in each step add up over many steps.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg agt" data-agt>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Steps in the task <input class="pg-in" type="range" min="1" max="20" step="1" value="8" data-n /> <b data-nv></b></label>
      <label>Success of each step <input class="pg-in" type="range" min="80" max="100" step="1" value="95" data-r /> <b data-rv></b> %</label>
      <label>Check and retry each step <select class="pg-in" data-check><option value="0" selected>No</option><option value="1">Yes, one retry</option></select></label>
      <label>Tokens added per step <input class="pg-in" type="range" min="100" max="2000" step="100" value="500" data-t /> <b data-tv></b></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Chance the whole task succeeds</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Tokens read in total</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Model calls, on average</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
    </div>
    <span class="pg-note" data-verdict></span>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query } from '../playground';

  // Success = r^n, or (1 - (1 - r)^2)^n with one retry per step. Tokens: step k reads k x t, so the total is t x n x (n + 1) / 2.
  type Tone = 'good' | 'bad' | 'mid';
  const trim = (n: number) => String(Number(n.toFixed(2)));
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-agt]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const setBox = (i: number, value: string, note: string, tone: Tone) => {
      q(`[data-o${i}]`).textContent = value; q(`[data-n${i}]`).textContent = note;
      q<HTMLElement>(`[data-b${i}]`).style.setProperty('--c', tone === 'good' ? 'var(--good)' : tone === 'bad' ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--border)');
    };
    function draw() {
      const n = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-n]').value), r = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-r]').value) / 100;
      const t = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-t]').value), retry = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-check]').value === '1';
      q('[data-nv]').textContent = String(n); q('[data-rv]').textContent = String(Math.round(r * 100)); q('[data-tv]').textContent = String(t);
      const step = retry ? 1 - (1 - r) ** 2 : r, success = step ** n;
      const tokens = (t * n * (n + 1)) / 2, calls = retry ? n * (1 + (1 - r)) : n;
      setBox(1, `${(100 * success).toFixed(1)} %`, `${(100 * step).toFixed(2)} percent per step, over ${n} steps`, success > 0.9 ? 'good' : success < 0.5 ? 'bad' : 'mid');
      setBox(2, String(tokens), 'when each call re-reads the whole history, so cost grows with steps squared (retries not counted)', n > 12 ? 'bad' : 'mid');
      setBox(3, trim(calls), retry ? 'each failed step is tried once more' : 'one call for each step', 'mid');
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = 'Errors multiply across steps and cost grows faster than the step count. Checks, short tasks, caching a stable prefix and a step budget keep a long task affordable and reliable.';
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
